#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
"""Run the checks of a checkout and record the result. The record, not an agent's word, is the evidence.

  pm-check <worktree|.> [--full | --only engine|studio|integration|harness...] [--on-request] [--no-retry] [--list]
  pm-check <worktree|.> --checks ID [ID ...]
  pm-check <worktree|.> --stop

Runs the steps of the modules the checkout's changes call for, as pm-scope decides them (the same code,
_pmscope.py): the paths that differ between the checkout's commit and its merge base with its target (main, or
the issue branch feat/<id> for a unit of an issue that has one), plus every uncommitted change, each decided by
the first rule it matches. Before the first step it prints the decision: one line with the kind of run and the
modules called for, one line per called-for module with the reason. Kinds:
  diff   the branch has commits of its own: what its paths call for (a path no rule knows: every module)
  main   the head is main's commit or an ancestor (the main checkout, a new branch): the product modules
         engine, studio and integration; the harness guards are left out
  unit   the fast check of a unit of an issue branch: what its own paths against feat/<id> call for, except
         integration, which is left to the issue branch: its step is recorded "deferred" (0 s, no log)
  full   --full, or the changes cannot be read (no branch main, no commit shared with the target, git failed):
         every module, nothing deferred
  only   --only: the named modules; a partial run, which never passes
  checks --checks: single integration checks; never a gate (below)
--full runs every module whatever changed, and the tier full of the integration checks (below); it cannot be
combined with --only. The whole check of an issue is
pm-check on the issue branch's worktree: its paths against main, integration included, where the integration step
holds every check of no service and the checks of the services those paths touch (below).
A step of a module that exists and was not called for is recorded "not-needed" (0 s, no log); it never counts as
passed. A "deferred" step counts neither as passed nor as failed; only pm-merge into the issue branch accepts it
for integration. The steps, for each module that exists in the checkout:
  engine       cargo fmt --all --check; cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings; cargo test --workspace
  studio       bun run typecheck; lint; format:check; test:unit --fsModuleCache=false; build
               (a check's result is evidence about the commit, and Vitest's cache of transformed modules is
               keyed by each module's own text, so it can hold the result of an earlier tree)
  integration  tests/integration/run (the suite's own entry point), given the worktree's engine and emulator ports
  harness      .pm/bin/tests/run (the harness guards, issue 523: unittest discovery, under 30 s in all)
A module whose manifest is missing (engine/Cargo.toml, studio/package.json, tests/integration/run,
.pm/bin/tests/run) is reported as "absent" and does not count as a failure, called for or not. A checkout where
every module is absent, or where nothing was called for (only issue files changed), passes on a clean tree.
Each step's output goes to <checkout>/output/logs/check-<step>.log. The summary goes to
<checkout>/output/checks/last.json: {commit, dirty, full, on_request, passed, failed: [steps], scope, steps: [{name,
module, status, seconds, log}]}. `scope` is what `pm-scope
<checkout> --json` prints: kind, reason, main's commit, the merge base, the number of changed paths, per module
whether it was called for and why. `full` is true only when every module was
called for. pm-merge refuses a unit whose last.json is not a pass on the branch's current
commit, or whose steps do not cover every module the branch's changes call for (it decides that again itself).
Exit code 0 only when no step that ran failed, the tree was clean and the run was not --only.

Harness guards (issue 523). The harness step runs .pm/bin/tests/run with no argument: every guard of what a script
may delete, stop or remove, in under 30 s. A path of .pm/bin/ calls it; no other path does. Kind main and --checks
do not run the harness step.

On request. A check whose manifest row is labelled `on-request` is not part of a default run: the suite reports it
`not-run` with the reason "on request: not part of a default run; run it with --on-request" and counts it in
`checks.not_run`. --on-request starts the integration step, when the scope calls for it, as ./run --on-request, and
its retry the same way, so those checks run with the others; last.json records on_request true (false without the
option). It changes nothing else: not the scope, not which steps run, not what pm-merge accepts (a pass with the
option is a pass). --checks runs every id it names, on request or not (the suite starts with --on-request), and
cannot be combined with --on-request; --stop and --list ignore it.

The tier full (issue 482). A check whose manifest row is labelled `full` runs only in .github/workflows/full.yml,
which the owner starts, and in a local run the owner asks for: the suite reports it `not-run` with the reason
"full: runs only in the full run; run it with --full" in every other run, and no changed path calls it. The option
--full (not a kind full of changes that cannot be read) starts the integration step as ./run --full, and its retry
the same way; --checks starts the suite with --full, so an asked check of the tier runs. Either is passed only to a
suite whose tests/integration/run (read up to 1 MiB, as UTF-8) names --full: a checkout cut before the tier gets
nothing. No agent runs the tier on its own: a plan, a worker or the pm runs --full or --checks of a check of the
tier only on the owner's word. The integration step's entry gets `full_tier` {of, left_out}, copied from this run's
report.json (absent when there is none or it has no such key), and pm-check prints it after the step's line as
`  full tier          <left_out> of <of> left out`.

Services (issue 327). The decision ends with the services line of pm-scope (`  services     every service: <why>` or
`  services     <names, or "none"> (<why>)`), the selection _pmscope.select makes of the same paths with the work
tree's manifest and the merge base's, each the main manifest's rows and then each service's (issue 402). A path
under tests/integration/studio/services/<service>/ gives that service, as a path of its screens does. For kind diff,
when the selection is a set of services, the integration step writes it to <checkout>/output/checks/services.json
({"services": [names], "why": why}) and starts ./run --services <that file>, after --on-request when both, the retry
the same way: run then leaves out every check whose manifest row names a service not in the set (`not-run`, counted
in `checks.not_run`). When the selection is every service (a shared path, the kinds main, full and only, a unit's
deferred step) it starts ./run as without the option and removes a services.json of an earlier run. The integration
step's entry of last.json gets `services`, copied from the run's report.json of this run (null when every service's
checks were part of the run, else the sorted list); the key is absent when there is no such report. The record's
`scope` holds `services` as pm-scope --json prints it. pm-merge holds the entry's `services` against the branch's
own selection. --checks runs every id it names whatever its service, without --services.

Failed checks named. After the integration step ran, pm-check reads <checkout>/output/integration/report.json
when that step wrote it for the record's commit, and puts `checks` {passed, failed: [ids], error: [ids], not_run}
in the step's entry (null when there is no such report: then the output says `integration: no report of this
run`); the last lines before the verdict name the failed and the error checks, the first ten of each. The step's
status still comes from its exit code alone, and `failed` stays the list of step names.

Single checks. --checks runs only the integration step, limited to the named manifest ids: the suite starts with
--not-run and output/checks/checks-not-run.json, which lists every other id of the checkout's manifest,
--on-request and --full, so an asked check that is on request or of the tier full runs. --checks takes an id of the main manifest
(tests/integration/manifest.jsonl) or of a service's manifest
(tests/integration/studio/services/<service>/manifest.jsonl), the manifest every reader reads, main manifest first
(issue 402). It is refused (exit 2, nothing written) for an id that is in neither, a part of the manifest that
cannot be read (named), a checkout without the main manifest or tests/integration/run, and with --full, --only or
--on-request. It asks for room like every run that starts
the suite (Load, below), runs the step once (no retry, no flakes.jsonl line), logs to output/logs/checks-integration.log and
records to output/checks/checks.json and a timestamped *-checks.json (kind checks, passed false, the step's
`asked` {id: verdict}); last.json and the check-<step>.log files are not touched. Each asked check is printed
with its verdict, and the last line says it is a partial run pm-merge does not accept. Exit 0 when every asked
check passed, else 1.

Intermittent failures. A test step that fails (engine-test, studio-unit, integration, harness-test) is run once
more. When the second run passes, the step is recorded as "flaky": the run still passes, the first run's log is
kept as check-<step>.attempt1.log, and a line goes to <root>/.pm/run/flakes.jsonl, which the PM turns into an issue
file. So one intermittent failure costs a rerun of one step, not the unit's merge, and it is never lost. A step
that fails twice is failed. Format, lint, type and build steps are never retried. --no-retry turns this off.

Load (issue 478). A run that calls for a module that builds or tests the product (engine, studio, integration) and
exists, and every --checks run, asks for room before its first step: _pmlib.check_room judges the machine against
the limits of _pmlib (memory, swap, CPU as measured; an unknown reading is room) and counts a heavy run that started
under 60 s ago as no room (its load is not measured yet); the ask is taken under a lock, <root>/.pm/run/checks/
.start.lock, so two asks never start on one reading. There is no limit on the number of runs: with room the run
starts, however many already run. Without room it writes no record and no log, prints one line and exits 75:
  WAIT <n>s: <why>; running: <worktree> <step> (about <s>s left), ...; expected room at <HH:MM:SS>; <tail>
where <n> is the least any running heavy run still needs (the rest of its step, at least 30 s, then its later
steps, each the median of the step's last 20 recorded durations, 300 s for a step never recorded), the rest of the
60 s for a run that started under it, or 60 s when none runs. For a caller that is a registered pane the tail is
`end your turn: EVENT room <name> check <checkout> comes when there is room`, and the pane is remembered in
<root>/.pm/run/waiting.json: pm-watchd prompts it that line once there is room. For any other caller (the pm, a
terminal) it is `run pm-check again after it`. A run that calls for no product module that exists (harness only,
or nothing) never asks. Each heavy run is recorded in <root>/.pm/run/checks/<pid>.json (its checkout, its start,
the steps it will run and the one it runs) while it lasts; every step that ran appends {at, step, seconds, status}
to <root>/.pm/run/check-durations.jsonl (a --checks run as step `integration-checks`). A record (last.json,
checks.json) holds `waited` {seconds, asks}: the time from the first WAIT answer this checkout got since its last
start, and how many asks were answered WAIT; {0, 0} when none was (<checkout>/output/checks/waited.json keeps them
in between).

Processes. Each step runs in its own process group, recorded in <checkout>/output/checks/running.json while the
run lasts. `pm-check <worktree> --stop` ends that worktree's run and nothing else: SIGTERM to the recorded
pm-check, which sends SIGTERM to its step's group and SIGKILL to what is left of it after the step's grace: 60 s for
the integration step, whose run removes its emulator in its EXIT trap, ten seconds for every other step. --stop
waits for the stopped pm-check to end, and ends the group itself only when that pm-check has not ended within the
grace and the sweep's bound. Never stop a check by process name (pkill, killall): that ends other worktrees' runs
too. A pm-check that receives SIGTERM, SIGINT or SIGHUP stops its own step the same way and ignores a further one.

Leftovers of an integration run (issue 342). tests/integration/run names its run on its first line (`integration:
run <id>, emulator port <port>, ...`). When an integration step ends, by itself or stopped, pm-check sweeps that
run (_pmitrun.py): it removes, by the run's id alone, the containers labelled emuforge-it-run=<id> and those created
under one of the run's image names, the volumes labelled with the id or mounted by them, the networks of their
Compose projects that no container uses, and the run's images emuforge-it-product-<id>, emuforge-it-emulator-<id>
and aws-emulator:it-<id>; then the folders ~/.aws/emulator/<port>/ of the run's port and of its checks' emulators,
through pm-emulator-dir (rm --worktree for the checkout's own port, else rm --port), which refuses one in use. A
run's trap that finished leaves nothing to find. At its start every pm-check (not --stop, not --list) sweeps each
run an earlier integration log of the checkout names (check-integration.log, its attempt1 log,
checks-integration.log) and that <checkout>/output/checks/swept.json does not hold, unless running.json names
another live pm-check; a sweep is recorded there when Docker answered every call and nothing was refused. What a
sweep removed, kept or could not ask Docker is printed as `integration: leftovers of run <id> ...` lines; --stop
prints the stopped run's.
"""
import argparse
import datetime as dt
import fcntl
import json
import os
import pathlib
import re
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import time

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
from _pmlib import (CHECKS, ROOT, RUN, caller, check_room, end_check, note_check, now, record_duration,
                    wait_for_check_room)
from _pmscope import called, deferred, lines, manifest_parts, scope, services_file
from _pmitrun import SWEEP_BOUND, sweep_earlier, sweep_log

STEPS = {
    "engine": ("engine", "Cargo.toml", [
        ("engine-fmt", ["cargo", "fmt", "--all", "--check"]),
        ("engine-clippy", ["cargo", "clippy", "--workspace", "--all-targets", "--", "-D", "warnings"]),
        ("engine-test", ["cargo", "test", "--workspace"]),
    ]),
    "studio": ("studio", "package.json", [
        ("studio-typecheck", ["bun", "run", "typecheck"]),
        ("studio-lint", ["bun", "run", "lint"]),
        ("studio-format", ["bun", "run", "format:check"]),
        ("studio-unit", ["bun", "run", "test:unit", "--fsModuleCache=false"]),
        ("studio-build", ["bun", "run", "build"]),
    ]),
    "integration": ("tests/integration", "run", [
        ("integration", ["./run"]),
    ]),
    "harness": (".pm/bin/tests", "run", [
        ("harness-test", ["./run"]),
    ]),
}
# real AWS credentials and profiles never reach a check
SCRUB = ("AWS_PROFILE", "AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID", "AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY", "AWS_SESSION_TOKEN", "AWS_CONFIG_FILE",
         "AWS_SHARED_CREDENTIALS_FILE", "AWS_ENDPOINT_URL", "AWS_DEFAULT_PROFILE", "AWS_ROLE_ARN", "AWS_WEB_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE")


RETRY = ("engine-test", "studio-unit", "integration", "harness-test")  # steps whose failure can be intermittent
HEAVY = ("engine", "studio", "integration")  # modules whose steps load the machine
WAIT_EXIT = 75  # EX_TEMPFAIL: no room now; ask again after the wait the answer names
current = None  # the running step's Popen
current_step = None  # the running step's name
GRACE = 10  # seconds a step's group has between SIGTERM and SIGKILL when the step is stopped
STOP_GRACE = {"integration": 60}  # a longer grace: the integration run's EXIT trap removes its emulator (issue 342)
BIN_DIR = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))  # pm-emulator-dir is the sweep's, beside this script
this_run = None  # this run's entry in <root>/.pm/run/checks/ while a heavy run lasts
CHECK_ID = re.compile(r"[a-z]+\.[a-z0-9-]+")  # the form of a manifest id; nothing else reaches a file
NAMED = 10  # failed or error checks named in the output, per verdict
MTIME_SLACK = 1  # seconds: a file's time can lag the clock by a tick; a report older than that is not this run's
RUNNER_MAX = 1024 * 1024  # bytes of the integration runner read to see whether it takes --full


def fmt_s(n):
    n = int(round(n))
    return f"{n // 60}m{n % 60:02d}s" if n >= 60 else f"{n}s"


def waited_file(co):
    return co / "output" / "checks" / "waited.json"


def ask(co, steps):
    """Ask for room for a heavy run of `steps`. With room: record this run in CHECKS and return
    (readings, waited {seconds, asks}). Without: remember the asker, print the WAIT line and exit WAIT_EXIT."""
    global this_run
    CHECKS.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    wf = waited_file(co)
    with open(CHECKS / ".start.lock", "w") as lock:
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        readings = {}
        why, wait, left = check_room(readings=readings)
        at = time.time()
        if why is None:
            this_run = dict(pid=os.getpid(), checkout=str(co), started=at, steps=list(steps),
                            step=steps[0] if steps else None, step_started=at)
            note_check(this_run)
    try:
        w = json.loads(wf.read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        w = {}
    if why is None:
        wf.unlink(missing_ok=True)
        first = w.get("first_at")
        waited = dict(seconds=round(at - first, 1) if isinstance(first, (int, float)) else 0,
                      asks=w.get("asks", 0) if isinstance(w.get("asks"), int) else 0)
        return readings, waited
    wf.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    w = dict(first_at=w.get("first_at") if isinstance(w.get("first_at"), (int, float)) else at,
             asks=(w.get("asks") if isinstance(w.get("asks"), int) else 0) + 1)
    wf.write_text(json.dumps(w))
    expected = dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(at + wait).astimezone()
    runs = ", ".join(f"{pathlib.Path(c or '?').name} {st or '?'} (about {fmt_s(n)} left)" for c, st, n in left)
    me = caller()
    if me:
        wait_for_check_room(me["name"], str(co), me.get("issue"), why, expected.isoformat(timespec="seconds"))
        tail = f"end your turn: EVENT room {me['name']} check {co} comes when there is room"
    else:
        tail = "run pm-check again after it"
    print(f"WAIT {wait}s: {why}; running: {runs or 'no check'}; expected room at {expected:%H:%M:%S}; {tail}",
          flush=True)
    sys.exit(WAIT_EXIT)


def at_step(name):
    """Note in this run's CHECKS entry that it now runs step `name` (a name not among its steps is the one it has)."""
    if this_run is not None and name in this_run["steps"]:
        this_run.update(step=name, step_started=time.time())
        note_check(this_run)


def done():
    """This heavy run has ended: its CHECKS entry goes."""
    if this_run is not None:
        end_check(this_run["pid"])


def end_group(pgid, grace=10):
    """SIGTERM a process group, then SIGKILL what is left after `grace` seconds. True when it is gone."""
    for sig, wait in ((signal.SIGTERM, grace), (signal.SIGKILL, 2)):
        try:
            os.killpg(pgid, sig)
        except (ProcessLookupError, PermissionError):
            return True
        end = time.time() + wait
        while time.time() < end:
            try:
                os.killpg(pgid, 0)
            except (ProcessLookupError, PermissionError):
                return True
            time.sleep(0.1)
    return False


def grace_of(step):
    return STOP_GRACE.get(step, GRACE)


def on_signal(signum, _frame):
    for s in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGHUP):
        signal.signal(s, signal.SIG_IGN)  # a second signal never cuts the step's end or the sweep short
    if current is not None and current.poll() is None:
        end_group(current.pid, grace=grace_of(current_step))
    done()
    sys.exit(128 + signum)  # run_step's `finally` sweeps an integration step's run


def alive(pid):
    """Whether the process runs: it exists and is not a zombie."""
    try:
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except (ProcessLookupError, PermissionError):
        return False
    r = subprocess.run(["ps", "-o", "stat=", "-p", str(pid)], capture_output=True, text=True)
    return r.returncode == 0 and not r.stdout.strip().startswith("Z")


def stop(co):
    """End the run recorded for this checkout, and only that one. A pane may stop its own worktree's run; only a
    caller in the main checkout (the PM) may stop another's."""
    here = pathlib.Path.cwd().resolve()
    if here != co and co not in here.parents and here != ROOT and ROOT not in here.parents:
        sys.exit(f"refused: you are in {here}, not in {co}. Stop only your own worktree's run.")
    rec = co / "output" / "checks" / "running.json"
    try:
        r = json.loads(rec.read_text())
    except (FileNotFoundError, ValueError):
        print(f"no pm-check run is recorded for {co}")
        return
    try:
        os.kill(int(r["pm_check_pid"]), 0)
    except (ProcessLookupError, PermissionError, KeyError, ValueError):
        rec.unlink(missing_ok=True)
        print(f"the recorded run (pid {r.get('pm_check_pid')}) is no longer alive; record removed")
        return
    # The run's own handler ends its step's group, with the step's grace, and sweeps an integration run; this waits
    # for it, and ends the group and sweeps here only when the run is stuck past that.
    pid, step = int(r["pm_check_pid"]), r.get("step")
    os.kill(pid, signal.SIGTERM)
    end = time.time() + grace_of(step) + 2 + SWEEP_BOUND
    while alive(pid) and time.time() < end:
        time.sleep(0.2)
    stuck = alive(pid)
    if r.get("pgid"):
        end_group(int(r["pgid"]), grace=GRACE if stuck else 2)
    said = []
    if step == "integration" and isinstance(r.get("log"), str):
        if stuck:
            said = sweep_log(co, r["log"], BIN_DIR)
        else:
            said = swept_lines(co, r["log"])
    rec.unlink(missing_ok=True)
    print(f"stopped pm-check pid {pid} (step {step}) of {co}" + ("" if not stuck else
          f"; it did not end within {fmt_s(grace_of(step) + 2 + SWEEP_BOUND)}, its step's group was ended here"))
    for line in said:
        print(line)


def swept_lines(co, log):
    """The lines of the sweep a stopped run recorded for the run its log names (stop's report), or a line saying it
    did not record one."""
    from _pmitrun import lines, run_of, swept
    run = run_of(log)
    if run is None:
        return []
    entry = swept(co).get(run[0])
    if entry is None:
        return [f"integration: leftovers of run {run[0]} were not all removed; the next pm-check of {co} tries again"]
    return lines(entry) or [f"integration: nothing of run {run[0]} was left"]


def other_run(record):
    """Whether the checkout's running.json names a live pm-check other than this one: its run is not a leftover."""
    try:
        pid = int(json.loads(record.read_text())["pm_check_pid"])
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
        return False
    return pid != os.getpid() and alive(pid)


def run_step(cmd, cwd, env, log, record, name):
    """Run one step in its own process group with its output in `log`; return the exit code (127: not found)."""
    global current, current_step
    with open(log, "w") as f:
        try:
            current = subprocess.Popen(cmd, cwd=cwd, stdout=f, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                                       env=env, start_new_session=True)
        except FileNotFoundError as e:
            f.write(f"{e}\n")
            return 127
        record.write_text(json.dumps(dict(pm_check_pid=os.getpid(), pgid=current.pid, step=name, started=now(),
                                          log=str(log))))
        current_step = name
        at_step(name)
        try:
            return current.wait()
        finally:
            end_group(current.pid, grace=2)  # nothing a step started outlives it
            current = current_step = None
            if name == "integration":  # what the run's EXIT trap could not remove (issue 342)
                for line in sweep_log(pathlib.Path(record).parents[2], log, BIN_DIR):
                    print(line, flush=True)


def this_report(co, commit, started):
    """<co>/output/integration/report.json as an object, when the file was written after `started` for `commit` and
    holds a list of checks; else None. Nothing is guessed from another file."""
    rep = co / "output" / "integration" / "report.json"
    try:
        if rep.stat().st_mtime < started - MTIME_SLACK:
            return None
        data = json.loads(rep.read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    if not isinstance(data, dict) or data.get("commit") != commit or not isinstance(data.get("checks"), list):
        return None
    return data


def report_checks(co, commit, started):
    """The checks of this run's report.json (this_report) as [(id, verdict, message)] when each has the suite's
    shape; else None."""
    data = this_report(co, commit, started)
    if data is None:
        return None
    out = []
    for c in data["checks"]:
        if not isinstance(c, dict) or not isinstance(c.get("check_id"), str) or not isinstance(c.get("verdict"), str):
            return None
        out.append((c["check_id"], c["verdict"], c.get("message") if isinstance(c.get("message"), str) else ""))
    return out


def read_report(co, commit, started):
    """{passed, failed: [ids], error: [ids], not_run} of the integration step's report of this run, or None."""
    found = report_checks(co, commit, started)
    if found is None:
        return None
    return dict(passed=sum(v == "passed" for _, v, _ in found), failed=[i for i, v, _ in found if v == "failed"],
                error=[i for i, v, _ in found if v == "error"], not_run=sum(v == "not-run" for _, v, _ in found))


def report_services(co, commit, started, narrowed):
    """(True, value) with the `services` of this run's report.json: null or the list of names; (False, None) when
    there is no such report or its value is neither. A report without the key is of a run that knew no --services:
    null when the run was not started with the option (`narrowed`), else nothing is said."""
    data = this_report(co, commit, started)
    if data is None:
        return False, None
    if "services" not in data:
        return (False, None) if narrowed else (True, None)
    v = data["services"]
    if v is None or isinstance(v, list) and all(isinstance(s, str) for s in v):
        return True, v
    return False, None


def report_emulator(co, commit, started):
    """{version, commit} of the emulator this run's report.json (this_report) names, or None when there is no such
    report or either value is not a string."""
    data = this_report(co, commit, started)
    if data is None:
        return None
    v, c = data.get("emulator_version"), data.get("emulator_commit")
    return dict(version=v, commit=c) if isinstance(v, str) and isinstance(c, str) else None


def emulator_line(entry):
    """`emulator <version> commit <commit>` of an integration step's entry, or None."""
    e = entry.get("emulator")
    return f"emulator {e['version']} commit {e['commit']}" if e else None


def suite_knows_full(co):
    """Whether the checkout's tests/integration/run names --full (the tier full, issue 482): read up to RUNNER_MAX
    bytes as UTF-8; a suite that cannot be read, or is larger, is taken not to know it."""
    try:
        with open(co / STEPS["integration"][0] / STEPS["integration"][1], "rb") as f:
            data = f.read(RUNNER_MAX + 1)
        return len(data) <= RUNNER_MAX and "--full" in data.decode("utf-8")
    except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError):
        return False


def report_full_tier(co, commit, started):
    """The `full_tier` {of, left_out} of this run's report.json, or None when there is no such report or no such
    key of that shape."""
    data = this_report(co, commit, started)
    v = data.get("full_tier") if isinstance(data, dict) else None
    if isinstance(v, dict) and all(isinstance(v.get(k), int) and not isinstance(v.get(k), bool) for k in ("of", "left_out")):
        return dict(of=v["of"], left_out=v["left_out"])
    return None


def full_tier_line(entry):
    """`  full tier          <left_out> of <of> left out` of an integration step's entry, or None."""
    ft = entry.get("full_tier")
    return f"  {'full tier':18} {ft['left_out']} of {ft['of']} left out" if ft else None


def manifest_ids(co):
    """The check ids of the checkout's manifest, in its order: the main manifest's, then each service's
    (_pmscope.manifest_parts). Refuses (exit 2) when the suite or the main manifest is missing, or when a part
    cannot be read, naming that part."""
    suite = co / "tests" / "integration"
    for f in (suite / "run", suite / "manifest.jsonl"):
        if not f.exists():
            print(f"pm-check --checks: {f} does not exist", file=sys.stderr)
            sys.exit(2)
    ids = []
    for path, text, why in manifest_parts(co):
        try:
            if text is None:
                raise OSError(why)
            for ln in text.splitlines():
                if ln.strip():
                    ids.append(json.loads(ln)["check_id"])
        except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError) as e:
            print(f"pm-check --checks: {path} cannot be read ({why or type(e).__name__})", file=sys.stderr)
            sys.exit(2)
    return ids


def refuse_checks(co, asked):
    """Every manifest id of the checkout; exits 2 before anything is written when an asked id is not one of them."""
    ids = manifest_ids(co)
    known = set(ids)
    for i in asked:
        if not CHECK_ID.fullmatch(i) or i not in known:
            print(f"pm-check --checks: {i} is not a check of {co / 'tests' / 'integration' / 'manifest.jsonl'} or "
                  f"of a service's manifest", file=sys.stderr)
            sys.exit(2)
    return ids


def main():
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    p.add_argument("checkout"); p.add_argument("--only", action="append", choices=list(STEPS)); p.add_argument("--list", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--full", action="store_true",
                   help="run every module whatever changed, and the integration checks of the tier full")
    p.add_argument("--checks", nargs="+", metavar="ID", help="run only these integration checks; never a gate")
    p.add_argument("--no-retry", action="store_true"); p.add_argument("--stop", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--on-request", action="store_true", help="run the checks labelled on-request with the others")
    a = p.parse_args()
    if a.full and a.only:
        p.error("--full and --only cannot be combined")
    if a.checks and (a.full or a.only):
        p.error("--checks cannot be combined with --full or --only")
    if a.checks and a.on_request:
        p.error("--checks cannot be combined with --on-request")
    co = pathlib.Path(a.checkout).resolve()
    if a.stop:
        stop(co)
        return
    if a.list:
        for mod, (sub, manifest, steps) in STEPS.items():
            print(f"{mod:12} {'present' if (co / sub / manifest).exists() else 'absent ':7} {', '.join(n for n, _ in steps)}")
        return
    ids = refuse_checks(co, a.checks) if a.checks else None
    logs = co / "output" / "logs"; logs.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    out = co / "output" / "checks"; out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k not in SCRUB}
    env["AWS_EC2_METADATA_DISABLED"] = "true"
    ports = {}
    if (co / "output" / "ports.json").exists():
        ports = json.loads((co / "output" / "ports.json").read_text())
        env.update(EMUFORGE_STUDIO_PORT=str(ports["studio"]), EMUFORGE_ENGINE_PORT=str(ports["engine"]), EMULATOR_PORT=str(ports["emulator"]))
    commit = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(co), "rev-parse", "HEAD"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip()
    dirty = bool(subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(co), "status", "--porcelain"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip())
    record = out / "running.json"
    for s in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGHUP):
        signal.signal(s, on_signal)
    if not other_run(record):  # what an earlier stopped integration run left (issue 342)
        for line in sweep_earlier(co, BIN_DIR):
            print(line, flush=True)
    sc = scope(co, full=a.full, only=a.only, checks=a.checks)
    print("\n".join(lines(sc)), flush=True)
    if a.checks:
        checks_run(co, out, logs, env, record, commit, dirty, ports, sc, a.checks, ids)
        return
    calls = called(sc)
    mods = a.only or list(STEPS)
    held = deferred(sc)
    present = [m for m in mods if (co / STEPS[m][0] / STEPS[m][1]).exists()]
    cpu, waited = None, dict(seconds=0, asks=0)
    if any(m in HEAVY for m in present if m in calls and m not in held):
        steps = [n for m in present if m in calls and m not in held for n, _ in STEPS[m][2]]
        readings, waited = ask(co, steps)
        cpu = readings.get("cpu")
    else:
        waited_file(co).unlink(missing_ok=True)
    results, flaky = [], []
    try:
        results, flaky = run_all(a, co, mods, calls, env, logs, record, commit, held, sc["target"],
                                 services_file(sc))
    finally:
        record.unlink(missing_ok=True)
        done()
    finish(co, out, commit, dirty, ports, sc, results, flaky, cpu, bool(a.on_request), waited)


def run_all(a, co, mods, calls, env, logs, record, commit, held=(), target="main", services=None):
    """Run the called-for steps. `services` is the services file's object (services_file) when the integration
    step is narrowed to a set of services, else None."""
    results, flaky = [], []
    for mod in mods:
        sub, manifest, steps = STEPS[mod]
        if not (co / sub / manifest).exists():
            results.append(dict(name=mod, module=mod, status="absent", seconds=0, log=None))
            print(f"  {mod:18} absent")
            continue
        if mod in held:
            for name, _ in steps:
                results.append(dict(name=name, module=mod, status="deferred", seconds=0, log=None))
                print(f"  {name:18} deferred  left to {target}", flush=True)
            continue
        if mod not in calls:
            for name, _ in steps:
                results.append(dict(name=name, module=mod, status="not-needed", seconds=0, log=None))
                print(f"  {name:18} not needed", flush=True)
            continue
        if mod == "integration":
            services_json = co / "output" / "checks" / "services.json"
            if services is None:
                services_json.unlink(missing_ok=True)  # a narrowed run's file must not outlive it
            else:
                services_json.write_text(json.dumps(services, indent=1) + "\n")
        for name, cmd in steps:
            if mod == "integration" and a.on_request:
                cmd = cmd + ["--on-request"]  # the first run and the retry alike
            if mod == "integration" and a.full and suite_knows_full(co):
                cmd = cmd + ["--full"]  # the first run and the retry alike
            if mod == "integration" and services is not None:
                cmd = cmd + ["--services", str(services_json)]  # the first run and the retry alike
            log = logs / f"check-{name}.log"
            t = started = time.time()
            code = run_step(cmd, str(co / sub), env, log, record, name)
            first = None
            if code not in (0, 127) and name in RETRY and not a.no_retry:
                first = logs / f"check-{name}.attempt1.log"
                log.replace(first)
                print(f"  {name:18} failed once; running it again (first log: {first})", flush=True)
                started = time.time()
                code = run_step(cmd, str(co / sub), env, log, record, name)
            status = "error" if code == 127 else "failed" if code != 0 else "flaky" if first else "passed"
            results.append(dict(name=name, module=mod, status=status, seconds=round(time.time() - t, 1), log=str(log)))
            record_duration(name, results[-1]["seconds"], status)
            if first:
                results[-1]["first_log"] = str(first)
            if mod == "integration":
                results[-1]["checks"] = read_report(co, commit, started)  # of its last run
                results[-1]["emulator"] = report_emulator(co, commit, started)
                said, value = report_services(co, commit, started, services is not None)
                if said:
                    results[-1]["services"] = value
                ft = report_full_tier(co, commit, started)
                if ft is not None:
                    results[-1]["full_tier"] = ft
            if status == "flaky":
                flaky.append(name)
                with open(RUN / "flakes.jsonl", "a") as f:
                    f.write(json.dumps(dict(at=now(), checkout=str(co), commit=commit, step=name, first_log=str(first))) + "\n")
            print(f"  {name:18} {status:7} {results[-1]['seconds']:>7}s  {log}", flush=True)
            if full_tier_line(results[-1]):
                print(full_tier_line(results[-1]), flush=True)
    return results, flaky


def named_lines(results):
    """The lines that name the failed and error checks of each integration step that ran, or say it has no report."""
    out = []
    for r in results:
        if "checks" not in r:
            continue
        if emulator_line(r):
            out.append(emulator_line(r))
        if r["checks"] is None:
            out.append(f"{r['module']}: no report of this run")
            continue
        for verdict in ("failed", "error"):
            ids = r["checks"][verdict]
            if ids:
                more = f" and {len(ids) - NAMED} more" if len(ids) > NAMED else ""
                out.append(f"{verdict} checks ({len(ids)}): {', '.join(ids[:NAMED])}{more}")
    return out


def checks_run(co, out, logs, env, record, commit, dirty, ports, sc, asked, ids):
    """--checks: the integration step once, limited to the asked ids; its record is checks.json, never a gate."""
    suite = co / "tests" / "integration"
    listed = out / "checks-not-run.json"
    listed.write_text(json.dumps(dict(checks=[dict(id=i, reason="not asked for (pm-check --checks)")
                                              for i in ids if i not in asked]), indent=1))
    log = logs / "checks-integration.log"
    readings, waited = ask(co, ["integration-checks"])  # the suite builds and starts an emulator, whatever it is asked
    cpu = readings.get("cpu")
    try:
        t = time.time()
        cmd = ["./run", "--not-run", str(listed), "--on-request"] + (["--full"] if suite_knows_full(co) else [])
        code = run_step(cmd, str(suite), env, log, record, "integration")
    finally:
        record.unlink(missing_ok=True)
        done()
    status = "error" if code == 127 else "failed" if code != 0 else "passed"
    record_duration("integration-checks", round(time.time() - t, 1), status)
    entry = dict(name="integration", module="integration", status=status, seconds=round(time.time() - t, 1),
                 log=str(log))
    found = report_checks(co, commit, t)
    entry["checks"] = read_report(co, commit, t)
    entry["emulator"] = report_emulator(co, commit, t)
    ft = report_full_tier(co, commit, t)
    if ft is not None:
        entry["full_tier"] = ft
    verdicts = {i: (v, m) for i, v, m in found or []}
    entry["asked"] = {i: verdicts[i][0] if i in verdicts else None for i in asked}
    entry["messages"] = {i: verdicts[i][1] for i in asked if i in verdicts and verdicts[i][0] != "passed"}
    print(f"  {'integration':18} {status:7} {entry['seconds']:>7}s  {log}", flush=True)
    if full_tier_line(entry):
        print(full_tier_line(entry), flush=True)
    summary = dict(at=now(), commit=commit, dirty=dirty, full=False, passed=False,
                   failed=["integration"] if status in ("failed", "error") else [], flaky=[], cpu_at_start=cpu,
                   waited=waited, ports=ports, scope=sc, steps=[entry])
    (out / "checks.json").write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=1))
    (out / f"{now()[:19].replace(':', '')}-checks.json").write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=1))
    if emulator_line(entry):
        print(emulator_line(entry))
    if found is None:
        print("integration: no report of this run")
    for i in asked if found is not None else ():
        verdict = entry["asked"][i] or "missing from the report"
        first = (entry["messages"].get(i) or "").strip().splitlines()
        print(f"  {verdict:8} {i}{'  ' + first[0] if first else ''}")
    ok = found is not None and all(entry["asked"][i] == "passed" for i in asked)
    good = sum(entry["asked"][i] == "passed" for i in asked)
    print(f"CHECKS {'ok' if ok else 'not ok'} commit={commit[:9]} asked={len(asked)} passed={good}; "
          f"partial run (--checks): not accepted by pm-merge")
    sys.exit(0 if ok else 1)


def finish(co, out, commit, dirty, ports, sc, results, flaky, cpu, on_request=False, waited=None):
    failed = [r["name"] for r in results if r["status"] in ("failed", "error")]
    present = [r for r in results if r["status"] != "absent"]
    ran = [r for r in present if r["status"] not in ("not-needed", "deferred")]
    full = sc["kind"] == "full"
    partial = sc["kind"] == "only"
    passed = not failed and not dirty and not partial  # a run that called for nothing passes on a clean tree
    summary = dict(at=now(), commit=commit, dirty=dirty, full=full, on_request=on_request, passed=passed, failed=failed,
                   flaky=flaky, cpu_at_start=cpu, waited=waited or dict(seconds=0, asks=0), ports=ports, scope=sc,
                   steps=results)
    (out / "last.json").write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=1))
    (out / f"{now()[:19].replace(':', '')}.json").write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=1))
    notes = []
    if dirty:
        notes.append("uncommitted changes: commit, then run again")
    if partial:
        notes.append("partial run (--only): not accepted by pm-merge")
    if not present:
        notes.append("nothing to run in this checkout")
    elif not ran:
        notes.append("nothing was called for")
    if flaky:
        notes.append(f"flaky (failed once, passed on the second run): {', '.join(flaky)}; recorded in .pm/run/flakes.jsonl")
    for ln in named_lines(results):
        print(ln)
    print(f"{'PASSED' if passed else 'NOT PASSED'} commit={commit[:9]} scope={sc['kind']} failed={failed or '-'} {'; '.join(notes)}")
    sys.exit(0 if passed else 1)


main()
